This is a DNS Filter Proxy written in Java.
It can be used for filtering ads and other unwished hosts based on Host Name filtering.

Please see dnsfilter.conf for settings and their documentation.


*********ANDROID-VERSION**********

- Requires Android 4.2 or newer.
- Install DNSFilter.apk from the zip package on your Android device.
- Start the App "personalDNSfilter"

On Android devices, dnsfilter.conf is stored in the app's PersonalDNSFilter folder.
In case you need to edit configuration on Android, you can adjust settings in the UI or edit dnsfilter.conf.

************PC-VERSION************

- You need to have Java (JRE 8 or newer) installed.
- First unzip!
- To run the program:

  => NOTE: Admin/root rights (or CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE on Linux) are needed to bind port 53 (DNS Server).
  => Within the install folder run "./start.sh" (Linux/macOS) or "start.bat" (Windows),
     or "java -classpath ./personalDNSfilter.jar dnsfilter.DNSFilterProxy".
  => Depending on the operating system, see Linux-Scripts/ or Windows-Scripts/ to set up autostart.

- For configuration of the software there are 2 options (the default configuration already fits most users):

  => directly edit the conf file
  => use the Android app to remote control (see 'how-to-remote-control' for details)

- To use the software, configure your device or router to use it as DNS server:
  For local use on the PC only, set your DNS server to 127.0.0.1 / ::1.
  You might even configure your router to use this as DNS server across your network.


For further documentation refer to https://www.zenz-solutions.de/personaldnsfilter
